# Meridian — generated from tracked files (spec frontmatter, goals/, decisions/).
# Committing it protected nothing and conflicted on nearly every merge.
specs/REGISTRY.md

# Generated artifacts. ADR 003: commit what a human reviews, regenerate what a
# machine consumes — generated/workspaces/*.json IS committed.
generated/data/

# data/ IS committed (ADR 007): 215 gzipped CSVs, 2.3 MB, plus the DDL and the manifest.
# Nobody reviews 53,902 order lines, so ADR 003's rule does not obviously cover it — the
# reason is durability, not review. The rows previously existed only in a bucket this
# project does not own and cannot read; committing removes that dependency rather than
# relocating it. data/.staging/ is the custody script's scratch area and is not.
data/.staging/

# Runtime output
backups/
reports/

